r on the beat sheet). 90s films stay in graph view. Occupancy is a chip at the top of the widget list, not over Run. This is **not** `studio-ui` and not a second product. See ComfyUI Apps."],[1941,"The same slices GitHub Actions runs"],[3445,"The sampler does not paint a PNG directly. It denoises a **latent** tensor. Width, height, and frame count are latent widgets."],[2928,"The start still owns look. Do not prompt audio (silent)"],[3299,"The stay-on-`:8188` loop (Klein → overlay-qc → TRELLIS)"],[3561,"The still → silent 5 s → AV 12 s loop"],[1447,"The stitched MP4 is **already on disk**: `${COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR}/ez_gosee_90s.mp4` (container `/outputs`), plus `ez_gosee_90s.html`. A **90s film ready** overlay offers play and download. Optional board: `docker compose --profile studio-ui up studio-ui` then http\\://localhost:8190/watch/gosee"],[3348,"The studio canvas uses Nodes 2.0 (Vue DOM nodes, not LiteGraph canvas drawing). `start` writes `Comfy.VueNodes.Enabled` and `Comfy.VueNodes.AutoScaleLayout` into `user/default/comfy.settings.json` **only when those keys are absent** — an operator who already toggled Nodes 2.0 off keeps that choice. Lab graphs stamp `extra.workflowRendererVersion&#x60; as &#x2A;*`Vue-corrected`** so coordinates stay LiteGraph-canonical; do **not** stamp `\"Vue\"` or the frontend shrinks the layout by 1.2×. Shipped node positions already leave room for Vue widget height (Enhance, CLIP, LoadImage, KSampler) so Auto-scale does not stack boxes."],[3392,"The T2I tour remembers the place in prose (`HOUSE IDENTITY` + Prompt Join `lock=view`). The clay tour remembers it as geometry: Blender dumps ten Workbench stills from named cameras, then Klein **edit** restyles each plate."],[3427,"The three-part engine: text encoder, denoiser, VAE"],[3989,"The writing-desk CLI mode is &#x2A;*`llm-desk`**. In-canvas **Creative Research** DESCRIPTION says occupancy **llm**: GPU 35B sidecar when `llm-desk` is up, else on-box 4B. Custom nodes · ComfyUI Apps."],[2081,